  "description": "The high-level ASP.NET Core integration for post-quantum JWT authentication. Add one line — AddPostQuantumJwtBearer() — and hybrid ML-DSA-65 + X-Wing tokens authenticate through the standard ASP.NET Core pipeline exactly the way AddJwtBearer always has: same AuthenticationBuilder, same [Authorize], same ClaimsPrincipal. Fail-closed by construction, AOT-compatible, observable via System.Diagnostics (Metrics + ActivitySource). This is the application-layer wiring (handler, options, four event hooks, JWKS-equivalent key ring, hosted-service warmup) — NOT a cryptography library. The actual ML-DSA / X-Wing / AES-GCM work happens in PostQuantum.Jwt and the .NET 10 BCL primitives; we sit on top of them. Distributed single-use-jti enforcement available via the companion PostQuantum.AspNetCore.RedisReplayCache package. Preview release — the API surface is what we expect to ship in 1.0; the cryptographic construction is not yet independently audited. See KNOWN-GAPS.md before depending on this for anything that matters.",
