  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "1.0.0-preview.2: Bug-fix preview on the 1.0.0-preview.1 surface. (1) PostQuantumJwtBearerMessageReceivedContext now exposes a settable Result property; setting it short-circuits the handler so OnMessageReceived can return AuthenticateResult.NoResult() or AuthenticateResult.Fail(...) directly — matches the stock Microsoft.AspNetCore.Authentication.JwtBearer pattern. (2) PostQuantumJwtBearerTokenValidatedContext gains the same Result property — lets the OnTokenValidated handler reject a cryptographically valid token based on custom authorization rules. (3) The challenge step now appends to WWW-Authenticate rather than overwriting it, so other middleware's challenge headers (e.g. Basic from a different scheme) survive the post-quantum bearer challenge. Three new tests cover each fix; full suite is 69/69 green. Same API stability promise, same audit-pending status as preview.1 — see KNOWN-GAPS.md. Full notes: https://github.com/systemslibrarian/postquantum-aspnetcore/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md.",
